 "title": "Dynamic Band Splitting releases adaptive audio-separation code and models",
 "summary": "Dynamic Band Splitting provides code and pretrained DBS-BSRNN and DBS-TIGER models for estimating music, sound effects, and speech from 44.1 kHz monaural audio, with an interactive listening studio.",
 "research_notes": "Clone the repository, install a machine-appropriate PyTorch build, then install the documented requirements and editable package.\n\nLoad DBS-BSRNN for the released 3-second, 1.5-second-hop recipe, or DBS-TIGER for the 6-second, 3-second-hop recipe.\n\nProvide 44.1 kHz audio, convert a multichannel input to mono if following the documented example, then call the separation API to obtain music, sound-effects, and speech estimates.\n\nMatch checkpoint architecture and chunking recipe: use 3-second windows with DBS-BSRNN and 6-second windows with DBS-TIGER.\n\nTreat demo and inferred stems as estimates rather than ground truth; inspect for source leakage and artifacts before downstream use.",
